We just need to check that $TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i)$ preserves the relations on $TL_{|P|}$ and $TL_{|P|+1}$. More precisely, we need to check
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i^2) = (-A^2-A^{-2})TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i)$.
        \item $TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i e_{i+1} e_i) = TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i)$.
        \item $TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i e_{i-1} e_i)= TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i)$.
        \item $TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_i e_j)  = TL(\iota_P^Q)(e_j e_i)$ for $|i-j| \geq 2$.
    \end{enumerate}

    If $TL(\iota_P^Q)$ doesn't introduce crossings, the above equations clearly hold. Otherwise, they follow from the Kauffman bracket interpretation of $TL(\iota_P^Q)$, combined with the fact that the Kauffman bracket is an invariant under regular isotopy and Reidemeister II moves (see Figure \ref{fig:relations-with-trivial-strand}).

