Let $\theta, \gamma$ be two elements in $TL_{\vec{F}}$, and let $b = [P, \alpha, f]$ be any element in $B_{\vec{F}}$. Then we have $\langle J_{\vec{F}}(b)\theta,  J_{\vec{F}}(b)\gamma \rangle = \mathfrak{tr}(\gamma^*J_{\vec{F}}(b)^*J_{\vec{F}}(b) \theta)$. Note that
    \begin{align*}
        J_{\vec{F}}(b)^*J_{\vec{F}}(b) = [f^{-1}(P), J_{|P|}(\alpha)^*, f^{-1}][P, J_{|P|}(\alpha), f] = [P, J_{|P|}(\alpha)^*J_{|P|}(\alpha) ,e]
    \end{align*}

    Here $J_{|P|}: Br_{|P|} \to TL_{|P|}$ is the classical Jones representation of the braid group $Br_{|P|}$, so we have $J_{|P|}(\alpha)^*J_{|P|}(\alpha) = J_{|P|}(\alpha^*\alpha) = J_{|P|}(id) = id$. Thus $\langle J_{\vec{F}}(b)\theta,  J_{\vec{F}}(b)\gamma \rangle = \mathfrak{tr}(\gamma^* [P, id, e] \theta) = \mathfrak{tr}(\gamma^* \theta) = \langle \theta,  \gamma \rangle$.

First note that it suffices to prove the case for $\sigma_1=+$, otherwise we consider the sequence $(-\sigma_1, -\sigma_2,\cdots,-\sigma_n )$.

If $\sigma_i=+$ for all $1\leq i \leq n$, then we consider the tree  $T_n^+$ whose  vertex $v_n$ is the root (degree 2 vertex), with all other vertices $v_j$ lying on the left edge of the root (Figure \ref{fig:all-left-tree}).

